Body:
Follow-up with the complete validator output for a **neutral** config (generic provider/model names, everything else taken verbatim from the V2 docs — including `experimental.subagent_depth` and model-level `reasoning_efforts`, which the original report also saw flagged):

<details>
<summary>Neutral test config</summary>

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permissions": [{ "action": "shell", "resource": "git push *", "effect": "ask" }],
  "skills": ["./team-skills"],
  "experimental": { "subagent_depth": 3 },
  "provider": {
    "my-provider": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "models": {
        "model-a": {
          "name": "Model A",
          "reasoning_efforts": ["low", "medium", "high"]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "mcp": {
    "timeout": { "startup": 45000, "catalog": 30000, "execution": 600000 },
    "servers": {
      "everything": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": ["npx", "-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything"]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Full <code>jsonschema</code> Draft202012Validator output — 6 errors, zero warnings from the runtime itself</summary>

```text
/
    -> Additional properties are not allowed ('permissions' was unexpected)
/experimental
    -> Additional properties are not allowed ('subagent_depth' was unexpected)
/mcp/servers
    -> {'everything': {'type': 'local', 'command': ['npx', '-y', '@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything']}} is not valid under any of the given schemas
/mcp/timeout
    -> {'startup': 45000, 'catalog': 30000, 'execution': 600000} is not valid under any of the given schemas
/provider/my-provider/models/model-a
    -> Additional properties are not allowed ('reasoning_efforts' was unexpected)
/skills
    -> ['./team-skills'] is not of type 'object'
```

</details>

Meanwhile `opencode2 debug config` exits 0 on this exact file and `opencode2 mcp list` connects the server — so every flagged field is accepted and honored by the beta runtime.
